# Authentication System Test Endpoints
# Use this file with REST Client extension in VS Code or similar HTTP client

### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001
@email = test@example.com

### 1. Register a new user
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/create-user
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "full_name": "Test User",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "phone_number": "+1234567890",
  "is_service_provider": true,
  "experience": "Intermediate",
  "availability": "Weekends",
  "about_you": "Test user for authentication",
  "category": "Testing",
  "longitude": "0.0",
  "latitude": "0.0",
  "locationName": "Test Location",
  "workSamples": []
}

### 2. Login (Send OTP)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}"
}

### 3. Verify OTP and Get Tokens
# Replace OTP with the actual OTP received
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "otp": "123456"
}

### 4. Access Protected Route
# Replace with actual access token from step 3
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

### 5. Refresh Tokens
# This will use the HTTP-only cookie automatically
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

### 6. Refresh Tokens (Alternative with body)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "YOUR_REFRESH_TOKEN_HERE"
}

### 7. Get User by ID
# Replace with actual access token and user ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/user/1
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

### 8. Logout
# Replace with actual access token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

### 9. Logout from All Devices
# Replace with actual access token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout-all
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

### 10. Test Protected Route (Should fail without token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### 11. Test with Invalid Token (Should fail)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer invalid_token_here